  "strategy": "<variables_and_objective>\nThe problem requires minimizing the overlap integral C_5 = max<sub>k</sub> \u222b<sub>0</sub><sup>2</sup> h(x) (1 - h(x+k)) dx for a step function h on [0,2] with exactly 303 ones in a 606-point discretization. This is equivalent to minimizing the maximum shift correlation between h and its complement.\n\nVariables:\n- h[i] \u2208 {0, 1} for i = 0 to 605, ensuring exactly 303 ones\n\nObjective:\n- Minimize C_5 = max<sub>k</sub> (2.0/606) * \u2211<sub>i=0</sub><sup>605</sup> h[i] * (1 - h[i+k]) where index wrapping is not applied, matching the scipy.correlate('full') behavior.\n\nConstraints:\n- h[i] \u2208 {0, 1} for all i\n- \u2211<sub>i</sub> h[i] = 303\n</variables_and_objective>\n\n<initialization_and_phase1>\nRepresent h as a binary sequence of length 606. Calculate initial overlap using scipy.correlate. \nInitialize temperature schedule with T0 = 0.5 and T_final = 0.001. \nAllocate max_iters = 100, with initial 1000 evaluations at each temperature.\n\nImplementation:\n\ndef compute_c5(h):\n    n = len(h)\n    dx = 2.0 / n\n    corr = np.correlate(h, 1.0-h, mode='full')\n    return float(np.max(corr)) * dx\n\ndef random_flip_move(h):\n    ones = np.arange(len(h))[h==1]  # Indices of ones\n    zeros = np.arange(len(h))[h==0]  # Indices of zeros\n    if len(ones) == 0 or len(zeros) == 0:\n        # Fallback: flip two random bits\n        i1, i2 = np.random.choice(len(h), 2, replace=False)\n    else:\n        i1 = np.random.choice(ones)\n        i2 = np.random.choice(zeros)\n    h_new = h.copy()\n    h_new[i1] = 0\n    h_new[i2] = 1  # Maintain sum by flipping zero to one\n    return h_new\n\ndef simulate_annealing(h0, T0=0.5, T_final=0.001, max_iters=100):\n    h_curr = h0.copy()\n    h_best = h0.copy()\n    T_curr = T0\n    best_score = compute_c5(h_best)\n    for _ in range(max_iters):\n        for _ in range(1000):\n            h_next = random_flip_move(h_curr)\n            next_score = compute_c5(h_next)\n            delta = next_score - best_score\n            if delta < 0 or np.random.random() < np.exp(-delta/T_curr):\n                h_curr = h_next\n                if next_score < best_score:\n                    best_score = next_score\n                    h_best = h_curr.copy()\n        T_curr *= 0.95  # Cool exponentially\n        if T_curr < T_final:\n            break\n    return h_best, best_score\n\nRun phase1:\nstart_time1 = time.time()\nn_init = 100\nparent = initial_h_values.copy()\nproject_feasible(parent, 303)  # Ensure binary and correct sum\nbest_solution, best_value = simulate_annealing(parent)\nduration_phase1 = time.time() - start_time1\n</initialization_and_phase1>\n\n<advanced_moves_and_parallelization>\nEnhance search by incorporating:\n- Change Move Probability (CMP): At probability p_c = 0.25, replace a region of bits from a window around a randomly chosen peak\n- Flip Move Probability (FMP): At probability p_f = 0.7, perform global random flips\n- Capture Strength Boost (CSB): Evaluate move quality by considering local agreement with best_solution\n\nImplementation:\n\ndef change_move(h, h_best, window_size=20):\n    center = np.argmax(np.abs(h - h_best))\n    indices = list(range(max(0, center-window_size//2), min(606, center+window_size//2+1)))\n    if np.random.random() < 0.5:  # Invert segment\n        h_new = h.copy()\n        h_new[indices] = 1 - h_new[indices]\n        return h_new\n    else:  # Randomize segment\n        h_new = h.copy()\n        h_new[indices] = np.random.random(len(indices)).round().astype(int)\n        return h_new\n\nAdd to simulation:\nif np.random.random() < 0.25:\n    move = change_move(h_curr, h_best, window_size=min(30, len(h_curr)//2))\nelse:\n    move = random_flip_move(h_curr)\n\n</advanced_moves_and_parallelization>\n\n<progress_monitoring>\nMonitor temperature, score distribution, and stagnation:\n- Check for stagnation if last 500 iterations show score improvement < 0.0001\n- Early exit if temperature drops below T_final without improvement\n- Estimate remaining time: budget_s - (time.time() - start_time)\n\nImplementation:\n\nstall_count = 0\nlast_score = best_score\nwhile time.time() - start_time < budget_s - 5:\n    # Check for stagnation\n    current_score = compute_c5(h_curr)\n    if abs(current_score - last_score) < 0.0001:\n        stall_count += 1\n    else:\n        stall_count = 0\n        last_score = current_score\n    if stall_count >= 500:\n        break\n\nAdd time check before each move set iteration.\n\n</progress_monitoring>\n\n<implementation>\ndef run(seed=42,budget_s=1300,**kwargs):\n    import numpy as np\n    import time\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\n    import random\n    \n    # Validate input dimensions\n    assert len(initial_h_values) == 606, \"initial_h_values must be length 606\"\n    \n    # Initialize solution with provided parent\n    start_time = time.time()\n    h0 = initial_h_values.copy()\n    n = 606\n    target = 303\n    \n    # Phase 1: Basic Simulated Annealing\n    if time.time() - start_time > budget_s * 0.9:\n        # Earlier termination if parent is unavailable or too complex\n        h_final = project_feasible(h0, target)\n        score_final = compute_c5(h_final)\n        return h_final, score_final, n\n    \n    h_best, best_score = simulate_annealing(h0, max_iters=50)\n    h_best = project_feasible(h_best, target)\n    best_score_corrected = compute_c5(h_best)\n    if best_score_corrected < best_score:\n        best_score = best_score_corrected\n        best_solution = h_best.copy()\n    \n    # Phase 2: Enhanced with CMP and CSB\n    n_cmoves = 3\n    for _ in range(n_cmoves):\n        if time.time() - start_time > budget_s * 0.8:\n            break\n        T_curr = 0.5 * (0.95)**_  # Reset to moderate temperature\n        for _internal in range(500):\n            if time.time() - start_time > budget_s * 0.6:\n                break\n            if np.random.random() < 0.25:\n                h_try = change_move(h_curr, h_best, window_size=min(30, len(h_curr)))\n            else:\n                h_try = random_flip_move(h_curr)\n            \n            try_score = compute_c5(h_try)\n            delta = try_score - best_score\n            if delta < 0 or random.random() < np.exp(-delta/(T_curr*0.8)):\n                h_curr = h_try\n                if try_score < best_score:\n                    best_score = try_score\n                    h_best = h_curr.copy()\n                T_curr *= 0.9  # Faster cooling\n        \n    # Phase 3: Final polishing\n    if time.time() - start_time < budget_s * 0.9:\n        dx = 2.0/n\n        # Repair for final check\n        h_best = project_feasible(h_best, target)\n        score_final = compute_c5(h_best)\n        \n        # One last refinement\n        h_temp = minimize(utility_function(h_best), bounds=[(0,1)]*n, method='COBYLA')\n        h_temp = np.clip(h_temp.x, 0, 1)\n        h_best = project_feasible(h_temp, target)\n        score_final = compute_c5(h_best)\n    \n    # Verify final solution\n    assert np.sum(h_best) == 303, \"Incorrect sum\"\n    return h_best, score_final, n\n\nAdditional helper functions needed:\n- utility_function to create a smooth version of C_5\n- project_feasible to ensure binary representation and fixed sum\n</implementation>",
